    LLM: 'Game: Truc. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Truc is a 15th-century bluffing trick-taking game from France and Spain. Players get 3 cards and try to win 2 of 3 tricks. NO TRUMP and NO suit obligation â€” highest card wins regardless of suit (7 is highest in French version). Equal cards spoil the trick. Major bluffing component: players can propose to raise stakes at any point.',
    objective: 'Win two of the three tricks in each hand. The first player or partnership to reach 12 points wins the game.',
